# ============================================================================
# Line endings are load-bearing here, not cosmetic.
#
# net_loader.lua verifies an Adler-32 of exactly the bytes raw.githubusercontent
# serves, and make_manifest.py hashes LF-normalised bytes. If a .lua file were
# ever stored with CRLF, every byte count and every hash would shift and the
# loader would reject the whole download as corrupt.
#
# `eol=lf` forces LF in the stored blob AND in the working tree, so the manifest
# you generate locally matches the bytes the CDN hands out. Do not remove this.
# ============================================================================
*.lua   text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf

# Everything else: let git decide.
*       text=auto
